  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "A cone has radius $r$ cm and height $h$ cm.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q6a",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "If $r=5$ and $h=10$, find:",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p21-q6a-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "the slant height of the cone",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$5\\sqrt5\\text{ cm}\\approx11.18\\text{ cm}$",
              "worked": "By Pythagoras’ theorem:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\ell^2&=5^2+10^2\\\\\\ell^2&=125\\\\\\ell&=5\\sqrt5\\text{ cm}\\\\\\ell&\\approx11.18\\text{ cm}.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 28
          },
          {
            "id": "p21-q6a-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "the surface area of the curved part of the cone",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$25\\pi\\sqrt5\\text{ cm}^2\\approx175.62\\text{ cm}^2$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\pi r\\ell\\\\A&=\\pi\\times5\\times5\\sqrt5\\\\A&=25\\pi\\sqrt5\\text{ cm}^2\\\\A&\\approx175.62\\text{ cm}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 28
          },
          {
            "id": "p21-q6a-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "the angle of the sector we get if we cut the curved part of the cone. Give the angle to the nearest degree.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{360}{\\sqrt5}^{\\circ}\\approx161^{\\circ}$\n\nThe sector arc equals the circumference of the cone’s base.",
              "worked": "The sector radius is $\\ell=5\\sqrt5$ cm and its arc length is $2\\pi r$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\theta}{360}\\times2\\pi(5\\sqrt5)&=2\\pi\\times5\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{360\\times5}{5\\sqrt5}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{360}{\\sqrt5}^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&\\approx161^{\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 36
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q6b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If $r=h$, find the angle of the sector that produces the curved part of the cone. Give the angle to the nearest degree.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{360}{\\sqrt2}^{\\circ}\\approx255^{\\circ}$\n\nUse $\\ell=r\\sqrt2$ and equate the sector arc to $2\\pi r$.",
          "worked": "By Pythagoras’ theorem:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\ell^2&=r^2+r^2\\\\\\ell&=r\\sqrt2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe sector arc equals the circumference of the base:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\theta}{360}\\times2\\pi r\\sqrt2&=2\\pi r\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{360}{\\sqrt2}^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&\\approx255^{\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      }
    ]
  },
